# 1. The gate: is there a finished order to assess at all?
#
# This is the one rule in the sample that stops on a *missing* precondition rather than on a decision.
# An unfinished order has no meaningful KYC verdict: the customer has not told us who they are yet, so
# listing seven missing documents would be noise on top of the one thing that actually needs doing.
# `stop` ends the run here, and the customer gets exactly one sentence.
#
# The `else` branch is where the stop lives, which is worth reading twice: the *false* case is the
# abnormal one. Written the other way round — `when orderStatus != "completed"` — the rule would say
# what it rejects rather than what it requires, and the requirement id would sit in the `then`.
#
# Schema: schema.yaml

rule "order-completed" {
  description "Nothing is assessed until the customer has finished the onboarding order."
  when
    orderStatus equals "completed"

  then
    satisfied "order-completed"

  else
    status "order-incomplete"
    message "Your application has not been submitted yet. Please complete and submit the onboarding form — we will start the review as soon as it arrives."
    requirement "order-completed"
    stop
}
